1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,618
Knees ache on the stairs, mornings stiff until you move - a few everyday foods could be feeding that joint inflammation.

2
00:00:05,938 --> 00:00:08,371
Soda, fried food, and deli meat are the big three.

3
00:00:08,691 --> 00:00:15,396
Women who drink one soda a day have a 63% higher risk of rheumatoid arthritis, found in a Harvard study of 80,000 women.

4
00:00:15,716 --> 00:00:26,236
Fried food throws off your omega-6 to omega-3 balance, and processed meat raises CRP, your body's inflammation marker - one study found 50 extra grams a day raised it over 38%.

5
00:00:26,556 --> 00:00:29,804
Swap soda for tart cherry juice, shown to lower CRP.

6
00:00:30,124 --> 00:00:35,705
Cut back on fried food and add a daily handful of walnuts for anti-inflammatory omega-3s.

7
00:00:36,025 --> 00:00:41,396
And swap deli meat for tofu or beans a few times a week - plant protein is linked to lower CRP too.
